INSERT [dbo].[DataSetColumn] ([DataSetColumnID], [DataSetID], [ColumnName], [ColumnType], [LogicalColumnName], [BusinessDescription], [ExampleValue], [Tokenise], [TokenIdentifierType], [Redact], [DisplayOrder], [IsFilter]) VALUES (254, 10, N'ham_a_2', N'dropdown', N'hama - ham_a_2', N'2. Tension 



Inability to relax, nervousness, bodily tension, trembling and restless fatigue', N'0, 0 - Not present | 1, 1 - Mild - occurs irregularly and for short periods of time | 2, 2 - Moderate - occurs more constantly and of longer duration | 3, 3 - Severe - continuous and dominates patient''s life | 4, 4 - Very severe - incapacitating | -99, -99 - Missing value', 0, 0, 1, 901, 0)

INSERT [dbo].[DataSetColumn] ([DataSetColumnID], [DataSetID], [ColumnName], [ColumnType], [LogicalColumnName], [BusinessDescription], [ExampleValue], [Tokenise], [TokenIdentifierType], [Redact], [DisplayOrder], [IsFilter]) VALUES (255, 10, N'ham_a_1', N'dropdown', N'hama - ham_a_1', N'1. Anxious Mood



Worries, anticipation of worst, fearful anticipation, irritability', N'0, 0 - Not present | 1, 1 - Mild - occurs irregularly and for short periods of time | 2, 2 - Moderate - occurs more constantly and of longer duration | 3, 3 - Severe - continuous and dominates patient''s life | 4, 4 - Very severe - incapacitating | -99, -99 - Missing value', 0, 0, 1, 900, 0)

INSERT [dbo].[DataSetColumn] ([DataSetColumnID], [DataSetID], [ColumnName], [ColumnType], [LogicalColumnName], [BusinessDescription], [ExampleValue], [Tokenise], [TokenIdentifierType], [Redact], [DisplayOrder], [IsFilter]) VALUES (256, 10, N'ham_a_guide', N'descriptive', N'hama - ham_a_guide', N'HAMILTON ANXIETY RATING SCALE (HAM-A) 



Below is a list of phrases that describe certain feeling that people have. Rate the patients by finding the answer which best describes the extent to which he/she has these conditions. Select one of the five responses for each of the fourteen questions. Please rate based on the past seven days

', N'', 0, 0, 1, 899, 0)

INSERT [dbo].[DataSetColumn] ([DataSetColumnID], [DataSetID], [ColumnName], [ColumnType], [LogicalColumnName], [BusinessDescription], [ExampleValue], [Tokenise], [TokenIdentifierType], [Redact], [DisplayOrder], [IsFilter]) VALUES (257, 10, N'bdrs_total', N'calc', N'bdrs - bdrs_total', N'Total BDRS Score', N'sum([bdrs_1],[bdrs_2a],[bdrs_2b],[bdrs_3a],[bdrs_3b],[bdrs_4],[bdrs_5],[bdrs_6],[bdrs_7],[bdrs_8],[bdrs_9],[bdrs_10],[bdrs_11],[bdrs_12],[bdrs_13],[bdrs_14],[bdrs_15],[bdrs_16],[bdrs_17],[bdrs_18],[bdrs_19],[bdrs_20])', 0, 0, 0, 898, 0)

INSERT [dbo].[DataSetColumn] ([DataSetColumnID], [DataSetID], [ColumnName], [ColumnType], [LogicalColumnName], [BusinessDescription], [ExampleValue], [Tokenise], [TokenIdentifierType], [Redact], [DisplayOrder], [IsFilter]) VALUES (258, 10, N'bdrs_20', N'dropdown', N'bdrs - bdrs_20', N'20. Agitation 



This item rates observed restlessness and agitation, although subjective reports are taken into  account.  ', N'0, 0   Nil (normal) | 1, 1   Mild (slight restlessness) | 2, 2   Moderate (clear increase in level of agitation) | 3, 3   Severe (marked agitation, e.g., near continuous pacing or wringing hands) | -99, -99 missing value', 0, 0, 1, 897, 0)

INSERT [dbo].[DataSetColumn] ([DataSetColumnID], [DataSetID], [ColumnName], [ColumnType], [LogicalColumnName], [BusinessDescription], [ExampleValue], [Tokenise], [TokenIdentifierType], [Redact], [DisplayOrder], [IsFilter]) VALUES (259, 10, N'bdrs_19', N'dropdown', N'bdrs - bdrs_19', N'19. Increased Speech



This item scores increased rate and quantity of speech or thought. It is predominantly an observer based rating, although subjective reports are taken into account. ', N'0, 0   Nil | 1, 1   Mild (slight increase in the rate or quantity of speech) | 2, 2   Moderate (racing  thoughts,  significantly  more  talkative,  clearly  distractible,  or  some circumstantiality; does not impede interview) | 3, 3   Severe (flight of ideas; interferes with interview) | -99, -99 missing value', 0, 0, 1, 896, 0)

INSERT [dbo].[DataSetColumn] ([DataSetColumnID], [DataSetID], [ColumnName], [ColumnType], [LogicalColumnName], [BusinessDescription], [ExampleValue], [Tokenise], [TokenIdentifierType], [Redact], [DisplayOrder], [IsFilter]) VALUES (260, 10, N'bdrs_18', N'dropdown', N'bdrs - bdrs_18', N'18. Increased Motor Drive



This item rates both subjective and observed increases in motor drive and activity. This should include both goal directed and non-specific activity.  ', N'0, 0   Nil (normal motor drive) | 1, 1   Mild (slight increase in drive, not observable in interview) | 2, 2   Moderate (clear and observable increase in energy and drive) | 3, 3   Severe (marked or continuous increase in drive) | -99, -99 missing value', 0, 0, 1, 895, 0)

INSERT [dbo].[DataSetColumn] ([DataSetColumnID], [DataSetID], [ColumnName], [ColumnType], [LogicalColumnName], [BusinessDescription], [ExampleValue], [Tokenise], [TokenIdentifierType], [Redact], [DisplayOrder], [IsFilter]) VALUES (261, 10, N'bdrs_17', N'dropdown', N'bdrs - bdrs_17', N'17. Lability



Observed mood lability or reported mood swings  This item rates both reported and observed mood lability.  ', N'0, 0   Nil | 1, 1   Mild (subjective reports of mild increase in mood lability) | 2, 2   Moderate (mood lability clearly observable, moderate in intensity) | 3, 3   Severe (marked and dominant mood lability, frequent or dramatic swings in mood) | -99, -99 Missing value', 0, 0, 1, 894, 0)

INSERT [dbo].[DataSetColumn] ([DataSetColumnID], [DataSetID], [ColumnName], [ColumnType], [LogicalColumnName], [BusinessDescription], [ExampleValue], [Tokenise], [TokenIdentifierType], [Redact], [DisplayOrder], [IsFilter]) VALUES (262, 10, N'bdrs_16', N'dropdown', N'bdrs - bdrs_16', N'16. Irritability



This item rates irritability and hostility. It is rated on the basis of subjective reports of irritability as  well as observed behaviour.   Reports uncharacteristic subjective irritability, short fuse, easily angered, manifested by verbal or physical outbursts ', N'0, 0   Nil | 1, 1   Mild (slight subjective irritability; may not be overtly present) | 2, 2  Moderate (verbal snappiness and irritability that is clearly observable in interview) | 3, 3   Severe (reports  of  physical  outbursts,  e.g.,  throwing/breaking  objects,  or  markedly abusive verbal outbursts) | -99, -99 missing value', 0, 0, 1, 893, 0)

INSERT [dbo].[DataSetColumn] ([DataSetColumnID], [DataSetID], [ColumnName], [ColumnType], [LogicalColumnName], [BusinessDescription], [ExampleValue], [Tokenise], [TokenIdentifierType], [Redact], [DisplayOrder], [IsFilter]) VALUES (263, 10, N'bdrs_15', N'dropdown', N'bdrs - bdrs_15', N'15. Psychotic Symptoms



This item rates psychotic symptoms, increasing from over-valued ideas through to overt psychotic  symptoms. Rate on the basis of interview and mental status examination. Some of the information for this item will have bee gleaned from previous items.   Presence of overvalued ideas, delusions, or hallucinations ', N'0, 0   Nil (absent) | 1, 1   Mild (mild overvalued ideas, e.g., self-criticism or pessimism without clear effect on behaviour) | 2, 2   Moderate (significant overvalued ideas with clear effect on behaviour, e.g., strong guilt feelings, clear thoughts that others would be better off without them) | 3, 3   Severe (clear psychotic symptoms, e.g., delusions or hallucinations) | -99, -99 missing value', 0, 0, 1, 892, 0)

INSERT [dbo].[DataSetColumn] ([DataSetColumnID], [DataSetID], [ColumnName], [ColumnType], [LogicalColumnName], [BusinessDescription], [ExampleValue], [Tokenise], [TokenIdentifierType], [Redact], [DisplayOrder], [IsFilter]) VALUES (264, 10, N'bdrs_14', N'dropdown', N'bdrs - bdrs_14', N'14. Guilt



This item rates guilt, self-blame and remorse for real or past events. Rating varies according to  extent to which person feels guilty or deserving of their fate.  ', N'0, 0   Nil | 1, 1   Mild (slight decrease in self-esteem or increased self-criticism) | 2, 2   Moderate  (significant  thoughts  of  failure,  self-criticism,  inability  to  cope,  or  ruminations regarding past failures and the effect on others; able to recognise as excessive) | 3, 3   Severe (marked, pervasive, or persistent guilt, e.g., feelings of deserving punishment; or does not clearly recognise as excessive) | -99, -99 missing value', 0, 0, 1, 891, 0)

INSERT [dbo].[DataSetColumn] ([DataSetColumnID], [DataSetID], [ColumnName], [ColumnType], [LogicalColumnName], [BusinessDescription], [ExampleValue], [Tokenise], [TokenIdentifierType], [Redact], [DisplayOrder], [IsFilter]) VALUES (265, 10, N'bdrs_13', N'dropdown', N'bdrs - bdrs_13', N'13. Suicidal Ideation



Thoughts or feelings that life is not worthwhile; thoughts of death or suicide ', N'0, 0   Nil | 1, 1   Mild (thoughts that life is not worthwhile or is meaningless) | 2, 2   Moderate (thoughts of dying or death, but with no active suicide thoughts or plans) | 3, 3   Severe (thoughts or plans of suicide) | -99, -99 missing value', 0, 0, 1, 890, 0)

INSERT [dbo].[DataSetColumn] ([DataSetColumnID], [DataSetID], [ColumnName], [ColumnType], [LogicalColumnName], [BusinessDescription], [ExampleValue], [Tokenise], [TokenIdentifierType], [Redact], [DisplayOrder], [IsFilter]) VALUES (266, 10, N'bdrs_12', N'dropdown', N'bdrs - bdrs_12', N'12. Helplessness and Hopelessness



This item assesses feelings of helplessness or hopelessness, gloom and despondency.  Subjective sense of pessimism or gloom regarding the future, inability to cope, or sense of loss of control ', N'0, 0   Nil | 1, 1   Mild (occasional and mild feelings of not being able to cope as usual; or pessimism) | 2, 2   Moderate (often feels unable to cope, or significant feelings of helplessness or hopelessness which lift at times) | 3, 3   Severe (marked and persistent feelings of pessimism, helplessness, or hopelessness) | -99, -99 missing value', 0, 0, 1, 889, 0)

INSERT [dbo].[DataSetColumn] ([DataSetColumnID], [DataSetID], [ColumnName], [ColumnType], [LogicalColumnName], [BusinessDescription], [ExampleValue], [Tokenise], [TokenIdentifierType], [Redact], [DisplayOrder], [IsFilter]) VALUES (279, 10, N'ymrs_total', N'calc', N'ymrs - ymrs_total', N'YMRS Total Score', N'sum([ymrs_1],[ymrs_2],[ymrs_3],[ymrs_4],[ymrs_5],[ymrs_6],[ymrs_7],[ymrs_8],[ymrs_9],[ymrs_10],[ymrs_11])', 0, 0, 0, 927, 0)

INSERT [dbo].[DataSetColumn] ([DataSetColumnID], [DataSetID], [ColumnName], [ColumnType], [LogicalColumnName], [BusinessDescription], [ExampleValue], [Tokenise], [TokenIdentifierType], [Redact], [DisplayOrder], [IsFilter]) VALUES (280, 10, N'ymrs_11', N'dropdown', N'ymrs - ymrs_11', N'11. Insight', N'0, 0 Present; admits illness; agrees with need for treatment | 0.5, 0.5 | 1, 1 Possibly ill | 1.5, 1.5 | 2, 2 Admits behaviour change, but denies illness | 2.5, 2.5 | 3, 3 Admits possible change in behaviour, but denies illness | 3.5, 3.5 | 4, 4 Denies any behaviour change | -99, -99 Missing Value', 0, 0, 1, 926, 0)

INSERT [dbo].[DataSetColumn] ([DataSetColumnID], [DataSetID], [ColumnName], [ColumnType], [LogicalColumnName], [BusinessDescription], [ExampleValue], [Tokenise], [TokenIdentifierType], [Redact], [DisplayOrder], [IsFilter]) VALUES (281, 10, N'ymrs_10', N'dropdown', N'ymrs - ymrs_10', N'10. Appearance', N'0, 0 Appropriate dress and grooming | 0.5, 0.5 | 1, 1 Minimally unkempt | 1.5, 1.5 | 2, 2 Poorly groomed; moderately disheveled; overdressed | 2.5, 2.5 | 3, 3 Disheveled; partly clothed; garish make-up | 3.5, 3.5 | 4, 4 Completely unkempt; decorated; bizarre garb | -99, -99 Missing Value', 0, 0, 1, 925, 0)

INSERT [dbo].[DataSetColumn] ([DataSetColumnID], [DataSetID], [ColumnName], [ColumnType], [LogicalColumnName], [BusinessDescription], [ExampleValue], [Tokenise], [TokenIdentifierType], [Redact], [DisplayOrder], [IsFilter]) VALUES (267, 10, N'bdrs_11', N'dropdown', N'bdrs - bdrs_11', N'11. Worthlessness



Assesses individual''s feelings of self-worth or self-confidence, compared to usual levels of self-esteem. Subjective sense, or thoughts, of decreased self-value or self-worth  ', N'0, 0   Nil | 1, 1   Mild (slight decrease in sense of self-worth) | 2, 2   Moderate (some thoughts of worthlessness and decreased self-worth) | 3, 3   Severe (marked, pervasive, or persistent feelings of worthlessness, e.g., feels others better off without them, unable to appreciate positive attributes) | -99, -99 missing value', 0, 0, 1, 888, 0)

INSERT [dbo].[DataSetColumn] ([DataSetColumnID], [DataSetID], [ColumnName], [ColumnType], [LogicalColumnName], [BusinessDescription], [ExampleValue], [Tokenise], [TokenIdentifierType], [Redact], [DisplayOrder], [IsFilter]) VALUES (268, 10, N'bdrs_10', N'dropdown', N'bdrs - bdrs_10', N'10. Affective Flattening



This item rates the intensity and range of the individual''s usual emotions. When giving examples to a patient, be aware that an example of feeling "unable to cry" may have gender specific  connotations  ', N'0, 0   Nil | 1, 1   Mild (slight constriction of range of affect, or transient reduction in range or intensity of feelings) | 2, 2   Moderate  (significant  constriction  of  range  or  intensity  of  feelings with  preservation of  some emotions, e.g., unable to cry) | 3, 3   Severe  (marked and pervasive  constriction of  range of affect or  inability  to experience usual emotions) | -99, -99 missing value', 0, 0, 1, 887, 0)

INSERT [dbo].[DataSetColumn] ([DataSetColumnID], [DataSetID], [ColumnName], [ColumnType], [LogicalColumnName], [BusinessDescription], [ExampleValue], [Tokenise], [TokenIdentifierType], [Redact], [DisplayOrder], [IsFilter]) VALUES (269, 10, N'bdrs_9', N'dropdown', N'bdrs - bdrs_9', N'9. Anhedonia



Assesses person''s reported ability to experience pleasure in usual activities. ', N'0, 0   Nil | 1, 1  Mild (slight reduction in pleasure from usually pleasurable activities) | 2, 2  Moderate (significant reduction in pleasure from usually pleasurable activities; some pleasure from isolated activities retained) | 3, 3  Severe (complete inability to experience pleasure) | -99, -99 missing value', 0, 0, 1, 886, 0)

INSERT [dbo].[DataSetColumn] ([DataSetColumnID], [DataSetID], [ColumnName], [ColumnType], [LogicalColumnName], [BusinessDescription], [ExampleValue], [Tokenise], [TokenIdentifierType], [Redact], [DisplayOrder], [IsFilter]) VALUES (270, 10, N'bdrs_8', N'dropdown', N'bdrs - bdrs_8', N'8. Anxiety 



Subjective reports of worry, tension, and/or somatic anxiety symptoms e.g., tremor, palpitations, dizziness, light-headedness, pins and needles, sweating, dyspnoea, butterflies in the stomach, or diarrhoea  This item assesses both reported levels of cognitive anxiety as well as somatic symptoms. The  presence of significant somatic symptoms usually reflects higher anxiety unless these symptoms  are due to another medical condition. ', N'0, 0   Nil | 1, 1   Mild (transient worry or tension about minor matters) | 2, 2   Moderate (significant anxiety, tension, or worry, or some accompanying somatic features) | 3, 3   Severe (marked  continuous  anxiety,  tension,  or worry  that  interferes with  normal activity;  or panic attacks) | -99, -99 missing value', 0, 0, 1, 885, 0)

INSERT [dbo].[DataSetColumn] ([DataSetColumnID], [DataSetID], [ColumnName], [ColumnType], [LogicalColumnName], [BusinessDescription], [ExampleValue], [Tokenise], [TokenIdentifierType], [Redact], [DisplayOrder], [IsFilter]) VALUES (271, 10, N'bdrs_7', N'dropdown', N'bdrs - bdrs_7', N'7. Impaired Concentration and Memory



This item examines an individual''s concentration, their ability to sustain attention and short-term  memory difficulties.    Subjective reports of reduced attention, concentration, or memory, and consequent functional impairment ', N'0, Nil | 1, 1   Mild (slight impairment of attention, concentration, or memory with no functional impairment) | 2, 2   Moderate (significant impairment of attention, concentration, or forgetfulness with  Some functional impairment) | 3, 3   Severe (marked impairment of concentration or memory with substantial functional impairment, e.g., unable to read or watch TV) | -99, -99 missing value', 0, 0, 1, 884, 0)

