CODE BASED ON INFORMATION ALREADY OBTAINED.', N'-99, -99 inadequate information | 1, 1 absent or false | 2, 2 subthreshold | 3, 3 threshold or true', 0, 0, 1, 317, 0)

INSERT [dbo].[DataSetColumn] ([DataSetColumnID], [DataSetID], [ColumnName], [ColumnType], [LogicalColumnName], [BusinessDescription], [ExampleValue], [Tokenise], [TokenIdentifierType], [Redact], [DisplayOrder], [IsFilter]) VALUES (1046, 10, N'scid_a_j_sum_b', N'checkbox', N'scid5rv_a_mood_disorders_j_premenstrual_dysphoric_ - scid_a_j_sum_b', N'Indicate provisional vs. definite diagnosis: (circle the appropriate number)

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

IF UNKNOWN: 

...Have you ever kept a diary of your symptoms and how they relate to your cycles?', N'1, 1 - Provisional dx: The symptom pattern in Criterion A has NOT been confirmed by prospective daily ratings during at least two symptomatic cycles. | 2, 2 - Definite dx: Criterion F is present, i.e., the symptom pattern in Criterion A (i.e., at least five symptoms must be present in the final week before the onset of menses, start to improve within a few days after the onset of menses, and become minimal or absent in the week postmenses) has been confirmed by prospective daily ratings during at least two symptomatic cycles.', 0, 0, 1, 315, 0)

INSERT [dbo].[DataSetColumn] ([DataSetColumnID], [DataSetID], [ColumnName], [ColumnType], [LogicalColumnName], [BusinessDescription], [ExampleValue], [Tokenise], [TokenIdentifierType], [Redact], [DisplayOrder], [IsFilter]) VALUES (1048, 10, N'scid_a_j_g', N'dropdown', N'scid5rv_a_mood_disorders_j_premenstrual_dysphoric_ - scid_a_j_g', N'G. [Primary Premenstrual Dysphoric Disorder:] The symptoms are not attributable to the physiological effects of a substance (e.g., a drug of abuse, a medication, other treatment) or another medical condition (e.g., hyperthyroidism).



Note: IF THERE IS ANY INDICATION THAT THE SYMPTOMS MAY BE SECONDARY (I.E., A DIRECT PHYSIOLOGICAL CONSEQUENCE OF GMC OR SUBSTANCE), GO TO *GMC/SUBSTANCE* A.45, AND RETURN HERE TO MAKE A RATING OF "1" OR "3."



NOTE: Refer to lists of etiological medical conditions and substances/medications on page A.4.



~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

...Since (1 YEAR AGO), when you were having these symptoms, were you physically ill?



IF YES: What did the doctor say?



Since (1 YEAR AGO), have you been taking any medications?



IF YES: Any change in the amount you were taking?



Since (1 YEAR AGO), have you been drinking or using any drugs?', N'-99, -99 inadequate information | 1, 1 absent or false | 2, 2 subthreshold | 3, 3 threshold or true', 0, 0, 1, 313, 0)

INSERT [dbo].[DataSetColumn] ([DataSetColumnID], [DataSetID], [ColumnName], [ColumnType], [LogicalColumnName], [BusinessDescription], [ExampleValue], [Tokenise], [TokenIdentifierType], [Redact], [DisplayOrder], [IsFilter]) VALUES (1049, 10, N'scid_a_j_e', N'dropdown', N'scid5rv_a_mood_disorders_j_premenstrual_dysphoric_ - scid_a_j_e', N'E. The disturbance is not merely an exacerbation of the symptoms of another disorder, such as Major Depressive Disorder, Panic Disorder, Persistent Depressive Disorder (Dysthymia), or a personality disorder (although it may co-occur with any of these disorders).



~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

IF HISTORY OF ANOTHER MENTAL DISORDER AND UNKNOWN: 



...Are these symptoms different from the symptoms you had from (PAST DISORDER)? Or is it just those same symptoms getting worse just before your period?', N'-99, -99 inadequate information | 1, 1 absent or false | 2, 2 subthreshold | 3, 3 threshold or true', 0, 0, 1, 312, 0)

INSERT [dbo].[DataSetColumn] ([DataSetColumnID], [DataSetID], [ColumnName], [ColumnType], [LogicalColumnName], [BusinessDescription], [ExampleValue], [Tokenise], [TokenIdentifierType], [Redact], [DisplayOrder], [IsFilter]) VALUES (1051, 10, N'scid_a_j_bc_sum_b', N'dropdown', N'scid5rv_a_mood_disorders_j_premenstrual_dysphoric_ - scid_a_j_bc_sum_b', N'Symptoms in criterion A-C must have been met for most menstrual cycles in the preceding year.



NOTE: Code "3" only if symptoms in criteria A-C have been met for 7 or more cycles in the past year.



